        "predicate": "summary",
        "object": "<p>£200,000 investment comes after harvests in Britain hit by wet winter, spring frost and hail, then heatwaves</p><p>The owner of Ribena is to invest £200,000 in helping blackcurrant bushes withstand stress after extreme weather put a squeeze on this year’s UK harvest.</p><p>That harvest is now under way in the berry’s main growing regions including East Anglia, Gloucestershire, Herefordshire, Kent and Scotland. It is expected to be about 10% below the average of 10,000 tonnes, as the climate crisis drives extreme weather across Britain and elsewhere.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/jul/17/ribena-owner-invests-uk-blackcurrant-bushes-extreme-weather\">Continue reading...</a>"
